  "world": {
    "_about": "The Night shop kit (task Д3, D61, D64, D106). colors: the code placeholders of the kit and darkness, the colour the dark room multiplies everything by (CanvasModulate). textures: a Gemini picture per piece, res:// path, empty draws the code placeholder; tools/cut_kit.py cuts them from docs/art/gemini/raw (kit_texel texture pixels per room pixel); brick, masonry and concrete repeat as tiles; floor_top and concrete_top are the flat top seen from above, squeezed into top_face_px (D109), floor_edge and concrete_edge the front edge under it, ledge_side the side of a ledge; column, pipe, truss, crane_beam and lamp_chain repeat along their length; crane is the trolley with the hook, lamp the caged lamp, both at their own size; machines and rubble keep their proportions, as wide as their rect and standing on its lower edge; soot, rust, cracks and stain are white masks painted with the colours of the same name (rust: rust_stain, cracks: crack); the rest fill their rect. brick_px: one brick of the placeholder wall; masonry_px and concrete_px: one block of the masonry and concrete placeholders, each dividing 256 (D112: the kit is sized to the heroine, 92 px = 1.75 m, about 52 px a metre; docs/art/scale.md). top_face_px: the visible top face of floors and ledges, her feet on its middle (collision unchanged). edge_px: the iron angle along the sides and lower faces of solid cells. machine_dim: background machines are this much darker than the wall pieces. lamp: every lamp of a layout (lamps in levels.json): the warm colour and energy of its light, radius_px of the island, below_px how far below the bulb the island's centre lies, flicker depth (0..1) and flicker_hz, a formula of world time; halo_px and halo_alpha: the soft glow round the bulb; picture_bulb: where the bulb is in the lamp picture, a fraction of its height from the top. heroine_light: a weak light that lights only the heroine, so she reads between the islands (D76). roof: the dark roof over the hall (ground.roof of a layout, D120). stairs: the picture of a flight of stairs (N-13) over its rect, empty: steps of the kit tiles, each about stair_rise_px high.",
